+## Failed session startup
+
+- If `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, the orchestrator awaits `onError(session, error)` and then `afterSession(session)` before rejecting with the original error, provided those hooks complete normally; both hooks receive the original session and `onError` receives the original error, and no user-input or model-response hooks run for that turn ([validated by: reports and cleans up a failed beforeSession before rejecting with the original error](../../src/orchestration/beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L7)).
+
+`afterSession` is cleanup for an attempted turn, including failed startup, rather than proof that startup succeeded. No additional startup-status argument is introduced: a deployer must track which resources its `beforeSession` acquired and release only those resources, because startup may have allocated nothing or only part of what it needs. This guarantee is specified by #94; its acceptance test remains red until that fix lands.
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
